 "bloques": [
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "This, that, that",
   "texto": [
    "**Isto** (this), **isso** (that) and **aquilo** (that) are used for things you don't name. **O que é isto?** = what is this?",
    "It is answered with um or uma: **É um livro** (is a book), **é uma caneta** (is a boli)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "The plural",
   "texto": [
    "The normal thing is to add **-s**: livro → livros. Those that end up in **-l** usually change the l to **-is**: blue → azuis.",
    "Those that end in **-r** or **-z** add **-es**: cor → cores, light → luzes. **-s** finishes usually add **-es** if they are acute (mês → months); if they are not, they usually do not change (or lappis → you are lappis).",
    "The ones that end up in **-m** make **-ns**: jardim → gardens. In **-ão** there are several plurals; look irmão / irmãos and pão / pães in the family lesson."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "The colors",
   "texto": [
    "**De que cor é?** = what color is it?",
    "They go behind the name and match: um car **vermelho**, uma mala **vermelha**. Blue and green do not change with the gender.",
    "Two false friends: «red» is **vermelho**, and **roxo** is «morado»."
   ]
  },
